- P2P rejection of foreign-domain proofs (CHK-0082): Is there anything in p2p_interface.go or batch_verifier.go that specifically validates the domain? Or does it rely entirely on cryptographic failure from ckzg4844?
- Validator domain consistency (CHK-0083): Is VerifyDataColumnsSidecarKZGProofs the single code path for all validators? Are there fallback paths?
- Domain separator construction (CHK-0084): Is b'RCKZGCBATCH__V1_' well-designed? Any prefix/suffix/truncation vulnerabilities?
- Hash input ordering (CHK-0085): In VerifyDataColumnsSidecarKZGProofs, indices are appended as sidecar.Index (same for all cells in sidecar). Is this ordering canonical and deterministic? What if sidecars arrive out of order?

